# NeXT plugin releases and versioning

## Manifest alignment

- **`ui/plugin.json`:** Keep `rrfVersion` and `dwcVersion` as **`auto-major`** (resolved to the DWC tree’s major.minor when the plugin ZIP is built). Rebuild against the target DWC line before release; a 3.6 build requires 3.6.x hosts, a 3.7 build requires 3.7.x.
- **When changing the dev/reference stack:** Update [`docs/RRF_REFERENCE.md`](docs/RRF_REFERENCE.md), [`README.md`](README.md), [`ui/src/index.ts`](ui/src/index.ts), and [`docs/UI_DEVELOPMENT.md`](docs/UI_DEVELOPMENT.md) as needed. [`docs/FEATURES.md`](docs/FEATURES.md) back-compat line tracks resolved `plugin.json` versions in shipped ZIPs.

## Gate before release commits or version tags

1. Run `./dist/build-plugin.sh <path-to-DuetWebControl>` from the **NeXT repo root**; confirm **exit code 0**. Use a DWC tree on the major line you intend to ship (e.g. 3.6.2 for 3.6.x).
2. **Manual verification:** Do not commit or tag a release until the user has **explicitly confirmed** the plugin **loads and works** in DWC on the target line (install ZIP, start plugin, smoke-test). Treat CI success as necessary but **not sufficient**.

## Tagging conventions (this repo)

- **Betas:** Increment **`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-beta.N`** (e.g. next after `v0.6.0-beta.3` is `beta.4`). Use **`git tag -a`** with a short message.
- **Stable:** Avoid **`git tag -f`** on an existing stable tag unless the user explicitly asks; prefer a new semver tag.

## CI

- [`.github/workflows/release.yml`](.github/workflows/release.yml) checks out **this repo only**; DWC is fetched as a **read-only GitHub archive** via [`dist/ci-fetch-dwc.sh`](dist/ci-fetch-dwc.sh) (pin: [`ci/dwc-build-ref`](ci/dwc-build-ref)). CI does **not** `actions/checkout` or push to Duet3D/DuetWebControl or any other external repository.
- Local `build-plugin.sh` + user sign-off remain the norm before tagging.
